        "title":  "Agentic AI is shifting the pricing models CIOs rely on",
        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/agentic-ai-outcome-pricing-models/829023/",
        "date":  "2026-08-31",
        "theme":  "Enterprise",
        "summary":  "Enterprise technology vendors are transitioning from traditional per-seat pricing to outcome-based billing models driven by agentic AI adoption, aiming to improve budget predictability by charging for completed tasks rather than usage tokens. Adoption remains limited with only 19% of service buyers currently using such arrangements, and CIOs must carefully negotiate outcome definitions and vendor accountability when considering these new pricing structures.",
        "execSummary":  "Agentic AI is forcing a structural shift in enterprise software contracts: vendors are moving toward outcome-based pricing where customers pay per completed task rather than per seat or per token, a model that could fundamentally change how AI investments are budgeted and evaluated. For customer-support leaders, this is directly relevant — AI agents handling ticket resolution or call deflection may soon be priced per successful interaction, aligning vendor incentives with operational outcomes for the first time. The critical negotiation point is the definition of \u0027completed outcome\u0027: poorly scoped contracts could result in vendors claiming payment for low-quality or partial resolutions. With only 19% of buyers currently on outcome pricing, early adopters have leverage to shape contract terms before these models become standard.",
